PHASE 1 MINIMAL SLICE: Historical Archive Merge

Goal

Implement the smallest safe version of “Import Historical Archive” that proves the merge model works without overbuilding UI or archive management.

Phase 1 imports messages from an external chat.db into the existing working timeline using GUID-based deduplication and provenance tagging.

⸻

Scope

This slice includes:

- Select an external folder containing chat.db
- Open the external chat.db read-only
- Analyze archive contents before import
- Import only messages that do not already exist by message GUID
- Tag imported rows with source provenance
- Return a summary to the user

This slice does NOT include:

- Attachment archive copying
- Per-source filtering
- Archive removal / rollback
- Full archive manager UI
- Fuzzy deduplication
- Contact merge refinement beyond current importer requirements

⸻

User Flow

Settings → Support → Import Historical Archive

1. User selects folder
2. App verifies folder contains chat.db
3. App runs preflight analysis
4. App shows:

Archive label: Messages_2012
Messages found: X
Already present: Y
New messages to import: Z
Date range: earliest → latest

5. User confirms Merge Into Timeline
6. App imports new messages only
7. App shows result:

Imported Z new messages.
Skipped Y messages already present.
Your timeline now includes messages from earliest → latest.

⸻

Database Requirements

Add nullable columns to the working message table if not already present:

source_provenance: text

import_batch_id: text

Default existing rows should be treated as:

source_provenance = current_mac

Do not rewrite all existing rows in Phase 1 unless the migration system already makes that trivial and safe.

⸻

Identity Rule

message_guid is the only dedupe key.

If archive.message.guid already exists in working DB:

skip

If archive.message.guid does not exist:

insert

No timestamp matching.
No text matching.
No sender matching.
No path matching.

