Initial Attachment Policy

Phase 1 should not attempt full attachment import unless the existing pipeline already supports it cleanly.

If archive attachments are detected, report:

Attachments folder found. Attachment import is not part of this first version.

If no attachments folder is detected, report:

No Attachments folder was found. Messages can still be imported, but older attachments may not be available.

⸻

Logging

Log:

- archive path
- archive label
- total messages found
- duplicate count
- new count
- import batch id
- imported count
- failed row count
- earliest/latest dates

Do not log message text.

⸻

Tests

Add tests for:

1. Preflight detects valid chat.db
2. Preflight rejects missing chat.db
3. Duplicate GUIDs are skipped
4. New GUIDs are inserted
5. Re-import is idempotent
6. Existing rows are unchanged
7. Existing overlay DB is untouched
8. Minimal legacy schema does not crash preflight

⸻

Success Criteria

Phase 1 is successful when:

- A copied historical Messages folder can be selected
- The app previews how many messages will be added
- The user can confirm import
- New messages appear in global timeline/search/heatmap
- Re-running the same archive adds nothing
- Current data remains untouched

⸻

Non-Negotiable Rule

This is not a replacement import.
